WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.500
(lighthearted music)

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.240
Jack Ma is Asia's richest man

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.070
and most recognizable business tycoon.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.640
He's the chairman of Alibaba.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.134
China's E-commerce giant

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:11.710
and one of the 10 largest
companies in the world.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.610
Yet he still wants more.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.530
We know where we're going,

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.790
we want to be the fifth largest economy.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.550
Big words from the man some
call Asia's Jeff Bezos.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.800
He's confident, he's charismatic

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.870
and he's definitely not the average CEO.

00:00:25.797 --> 00:00:30.797
♪ Can you feel the love tonight ♪

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:33.503
This is how a poor school teacher

00:00:33.503 --> 00:00:35.230
went from the classroom, to being one

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.982
of the most influential
multi-billionaires in the world.

00:00:37.982 --> 00:00:41.065
(lighthearted music)

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.450
Ma was born in China's southeastern
city, Hangzhou, in 1964.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.050
His parents were traditional
musician storytellers.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.430
As a teenager, he started to learn English

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.410
from foreign tourists,

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.400
after China opened up in the late 1970's.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.390
And then for nine years, Jack Ma,

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.640
hung around outside the Hangzhou Hotel,

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:03.550
which is now called the Shangri-La.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.970
He would get up at five a.m.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.300
to talk to travelers.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.420
That's Bloomberg Technology
reporter, Lulu Chen.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.720
And I cover China
internet for Bloomberg.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.070
Ma failed China's National University

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.153
entrance exam twice

00:01:16.153 --> 00:01:19.320
before being admitted to
Local Teachers College.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.290
He graduated in 1988.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.010
He applied for 30 jobs and got rejected.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:27.873
Including from the fast food giant, KFC.

00:01:27.873 --> 00:01:29.225
When KFC come to China,

00:01:29.225 --> 00:01:31.357
(crowd laughing)

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:35.397
24 people went for the job.

00:01:35.397 --> 00:01:38.470
23 people were accepted,
I was the only one guy.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.020
Then Ma got a job at a local university

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.210
and taught English there
for about five years

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.170
earning just $15 dollars a month.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.330
On the side he started
a translation company

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.510
with several friends.

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:55.620
During a company trip to the U.S. in 1995,

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.710
Ma had his first encounter
with the internet,

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.270
at a friend’s place in Seattle.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.045
I searched the first word, beer.

00:02:03.045 --> 00:02:05.530
(crowd laughing)

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:08.520
I don't why, because easy to spell, maybe.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.810
And I see beers from Germany,

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.630
beers from U.S.A, beers from Japan.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:16.250
But there's no beer from China.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.620
So he searched for the word China instead

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.370
and still couldn't find anything.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.200
And that got him thinking,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.330
he wanted to build something

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.410
that would put China on the world's map.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.080
He started China Pages,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.030
a Yellow Pages like website,
but it didn't take off.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.730
Then Ma joined a government agency

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.780
in Beijing to help set up a website.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.180
(energetic music)

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.550
By 1999, the internet stock boom

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.100
had gripped Wall Street.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.790
And back in his Hangzhou apartment,

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.700
Ma decided to try again.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.450
With his wife and a group of friends,

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.250
Ma raised $80,000 dollars,

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.140
and set up Alibaba, a site
that allowed businesses

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:53.516
to sell stuff to each other.

00:02:53.516 --> 00:02:58.433
(speaking excitedly in a foreign language)

00:03:02.546 --> 00:03:05.129
(upbeat music)

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.650
By 2000, Alibaba had
raised $25 million dollars

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.730
from investors, including
Goldman Sachs and SoftBank.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.230
He had no business plan

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.920
and zero revenue,

00:03:21.106 --> 00:03:25.630
but his eyes were very strong.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.500
Strong eyes.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.940
(laughing)

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:32.120
In 2003, Alibaba started Taobao,

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.820
a platform for individual sellers

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.090
to trade with each other

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.570
and publicly declared war against eBay,

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:39.980
who had started to make
a foray into China.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.440
Jack Ma has this famous saying

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.140
that Alibaba is a crocodile
in the Yangtze River,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.410
whereas eBay is a shark in the ocean.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.160
And if they fight eBay in the ocean

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.032
then they'll lose,

00:03:51.032 --> 00:03:53.340
but if they fight them
in the Yangtze River

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.202
then they have a home base advantage.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.785
(upbeat music)

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.700
In 2007, just one year

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.740
after it forced eBay out of China,

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.100
Alibaba debuted its
business-facing division

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.170
on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.970
But it delisted five years later,

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.347
as its performance sagged.

00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:12.486
(bells chiming)

00:04:12.486 --> 00:04:13.640
(crowd yelling)

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.410
In 2014, Alibaba raised
$25 billion dollars

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.950
in the world’s biggest IPO in New York.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.420
Everybody should have a dream.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.290
What if that dream comes true?

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.530
After achieving dominance

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.810
in the business of E-commerce in China,

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.150
Alibaba has been building

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:32.020
an internet empire worth
$472 billion dollars

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.120
with businesses in cloud computing,

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.760
online video streaming, movie production,

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.580
healthcare, sports, retail,
and even news media.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.730
Alibaba buying into
South China Morning Post

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.240
really raised eyebrows.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.500
This is the largest English
newspaper in Hong Kong.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.560
And it shows that Jack Ma's ambitions

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.680
weren't limited to E-commerce.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.040
He wanted to influence,
not just Chinese users,

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.714
but also overseas users, as well.

00:04:59.714 --> 00:05:01.270
(upbeat music)

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.020
The U.S. has criticized Alibaba

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.010
for allowing companies

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.280
to sell counterfeit and poorly made goods.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.040
But in China, it enjoys the favor

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.360
of China's government.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.110
It's part of Ma's company philosophy.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.410
In love with the government,

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.930
but don't marry with them.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.940
Jack Ma is an extremely fortunate man

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.500
for jumping on the
internet sector so early.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.230
Note that this is a person

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.370
who has no coding skills at all.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:26.370
He's a natural showman
and a gifted public speaker,

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.330
and really able to convince others

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.760
to believe in his vision.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.620
Ma's vision of growing Alibaba

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.610
to be the world’s fifth largest economy

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:37.734
faces strong competition
at home and abroad.

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:41.640
It will require more than just
naked ambition and charisma.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.490
But Ma is great at getting himself

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.770
in the right place at the right time.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.255
So far it's served him well.

00:05:47.255 --> 00:05:50.172
(successful music)

